celebrations on the streets of the  kyrgyz capital bishkek  after the president suramay jim beckhoff  resigned  it comes after more than two weeks of  chaos in a country  that has seen two other presidents  forced out in revolutions  in the last 15 years  [Applause]  unjust people were ruling the country we  got rid of them  inshallah now everything will be fine we  are happy  we want hooray ginbekov and  pro-government parties are widely  accused of rigging the october the  fourth  parliamentary elections the central  election committee  annulled the results and has called for  a rerun of the poll  but the man seen as finally forcing the  president's resignation  the new prime minister sander japarov is  considered by many  as a threat to what little remains of  this country's  fledgling democracy japaroff had been  serving an 11-year jail term for  kidnapping  before he was freed by supporters during  the recent  post-election protests  his supporters now want parliament to be  dissolved  [Music]  thank god people are happy now we're  calling for 120 lawmakers to make a  statement  for there to be a self-dissolution of  parliament because people don't want  them here they want siddhi yaparov to  take power and start working  because they only support him  just hours after president gene beckhoff  resigned the parliamentary speaker  who along with prime minister japan was  voted into office in recent days  refused to take up his role as acting  president  the refusal of the parliamentary speaker  to be interim president gives acting  presidential power to the new prime  minister  sadira japarov a man whom many in this  country  deeply oppose the political crisis and  uncertainty in kyrgyzstan  is not over yet charles stratford al  jazeera bishkek
 

